\[
\Sigma = r^2 + a^2 \cos^2\theta, \qquad
\Delta = r^2 - 2Mr + a^2 + Q^2.
\]

The horizon radii are
\[
r_{\pm} = M \pm \sqrt{M^2 - a^2 - Q^2}.
\]

The surface gravity, relevant for Hawking radiation detection, is
\[
\kappa = \frac{r_+ - r_-}{2(r_+^2 + a^2)}.
\]

